# Python 3.14 packages for scripts/unimedvl_server.py (issues #6, #21).
#
# Based on the pip section of codes/environment.yaml in
# https://github.com/uni-medical/UniMedVL at commit
# f51aa0accbd02e846e5ea20b595fb39b516dbe1f. Only the Jupyter packages are
# left out; the server does not use a notebook. Upstream uses Python 3.10.18;
# this runs on 3.14. sentencepiece 0.2.2 has no usable cp315 wheel, so the
# complete binary-only installation still requires Python 3.14.
#
# scripts/unimedvl-requirements.txt is the full lock compiled from this file
# (every transitive package pinned). Dependabot's uv ecosystem keeps both
# files up to date (.github/dependabot.yml). It compiles from scripts/ and
# keeps only --python-version, so compile from scripts/ by hand too, or every
# "# via -r" line changes in its next pull request:
#
#   cd scripts && uv pip compile unimedvl-requirements.in \
#     -o unimedvl-requirements.txt --python-version 3.14 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28
#
# Every package is at its newest compatible release (issue #25). torch 2.15
# pins cuda-toolkit 13.2.2 and the matching CUDA libraries, cuDNN, cuSPARSELt,
# NCCL and NVSHMEM exactly; sympy 1.14.0 requires mpmath<1.4.
# See dev/log/issues/25/pulls/26 for registry versions and held-pin reasons.
# Upstream was written for
# transformers 4.x and flash-attn; scripts/unimedvl_server.py
# uses transformers' maintained Qwen2 config and rotary embedding instead of
# restoring the removed RoPE helper, and serves flash_attn_varlen_func from torch's
# own varlen_attn, so neither transformers nor torch is held back any more and
# no flash-attn wheel is installed (flash-attn 2.8.3.post2 ships wheels only
# for torch <= 2.8 and Python <= 3.13).
# tests/test_unimedvl_upstream.py runs upstream's chat() on the CPU with a tiny
# model on this lock in CI (model-tests.yml, unimedvl-cpu), and
# experiments/issue21_unimedvl_cross_stack.py shows that torch 2.14.1 with
# transformers 5.20.1 gives the same logits as torch 2.8.0 with transformers
# 4.57.6 on the same weights.
# opencv-python 5: upstream calls OpenCV only in motion_blur_opencv (a training
# augmentation nothing calls); OpenCV 5 interpolates float images exactly
# where 4.x rounded to 1/32 pixel, so its blur differs by at most one grey
# level off the axes (experiments/issue19_unimedvl_opencv_probe.py).
# torchvision and triton are released with torch, and tokenizers with
# transformers: each release of the parent needs its own release of these
# (torch 2.15 requires triton~=3.9.0, transformers 5.22.1 tokenizers<0.24). Dependabot updates the members of a
# group one at a time (dependabot/dependabot-core#16390), so if both were
# pinned here neither could ever move. They are named without a version: the
# lock pins them, and Dependabot's update of torch or transformers carries
# them along (experiments/issue21_dependabot_lockstep.sh).
torch==2.15.0
torchvision
triton
transformers==5.22.1
accelerate==1.15.0
safetensors==0.8.0
tokenizers
sentencepiece==0.2.2
pillow==13.0.0
numpy==2.5.4
opencv-python==5.0.0.93
einops==0.8.2
matplotlib==3.11.2
contourpy==1.4.0
cycler==0.12.1
fonttools==4.68.0
kiwisolver==1.5.1
packaging==26.3
pyparsing==3.3.3
python-dateutil==3.0.0
